@startuml

salt
{
  <b>ORE STUDIO - REPORTING: AUTHOR A PRICING ENGINE CONFIGURATION</b>
  --
  {#
    Step | What it carries
    1 | name it, and choose where to start
    2 | choose the products
    3 | choose the model and the engine
    4 | set the parameters
    5 | check it
    6 | review and save (final)
  }
  --
  <b>STEP 3 - THE MODEL AND THE ENGINE</b>
  Each chosen product gets a model and an engine. The engine list narrows to the engines known to run the model.
  {#
    Product | Model | Engine | The usual | What the pair does
    Swap | ^DiscountedCashflows^ | ^DiscountingSwapEngine^ | [ Use the usual ] | discounts the cashflows
    EuropeanSwaption | ^BlackBachelier^ | ^BlackBachelierSwaptionEngine^ | [ Use the usual ] | prices by the Black or Bachelier formula
    BermudanSwaption | ^LGM^ | ^Grid^ | [ Use the usual ] | lattice on a calibrated one-factor model
    CapFloor | ^IborCapModel^ | ^AMC^ | [ Use the usual ] | MARKED: pair not known to work
  }
  A marked pair is a statement, not a refusal. No server check stands behind it.
  [ Back ] | [ Next: the parameters ]
}

@enduml
